WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.433 --> 00:00:02.002
-Congratulations on your haircut
in the movie.

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:03.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:04.404 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Thank you, yeah.

00:00:04.404 --> 00:00:05.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
They were like,
"We have a wig for you."

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:07.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "Wigs?
I got my own."

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:09.442
-Did you -- Now, did you?
-No, that was my hair.

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:10.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Really?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:12.245
-I was watching saying,
"That looks really good."

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:13.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you've got
a great head of hair

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:17.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I feel like can also look
awful as evidenced by that,

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:20.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
but that's great.
-It's called a period piece.

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:22.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I actually remember going
up to Kathryn Bigelow,

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:23.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
who is one of the greatest
directors ever.

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:25.091
And she was like,
"Yeah, just pull the hair down.

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:27.293
It's kind of the style." And I
was like, "Yeah, yeah, totally."

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:29.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I kept trying to sneak it
back for the scene.

00:00:29.496 --> 00:00:32.699
I wanted to do a lot of like --
"You know, Your Honor."

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:34.334
And she's like "No, no, no.
It's not how they wore it."

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:35.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"Okay, I'll put it back."

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:37.971
-Yeah. It's so weird to think
that there was just a time

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:40.673
where everybody was totally fine
with like just hair.

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:43.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, just like just resting
there your whole day,

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:45.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
a big old --
big old fat piece of hair.

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:49.215
-Just a nation of, like, skater
kids being like,

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:51.184 size:88% position:44% line:92%
"Hey I'm also a lawyer."

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:51.918 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You know?

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:53.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And did you know --
so this is --

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:56.556
You mentioned Oscar winner
Kathryn Bigelow directed and --

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:57.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I thought you
were talking about me.

00:00:57.657 --> 00:01:02.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "Oscar winner?
Let's not jump the gun.

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:03.463 line:92%
I'm feeling pretty good."

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:06.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
The hair will win.
-The hair will win, yeah.

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:06.966 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:09.702 size:84% position:42%
Did you know much about
these Detroit riots?

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:10.437 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-I had heard about it.

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:14.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had heard a little bit about
it, but nothing in detail.

00:01:14.374 --> 00:01:17.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's unlike anything else
I've seen.

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:19.579
To say it's the best movie
I've seen in a long time

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:22.182
is such an understatement
because it's almost --

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:23.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
When I came out of the
screening, this girl was like,

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:25.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You know, people are talking
about virtual reality.

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:27.387
That is virtual reality."
And that's what it is.

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:30.590
You're immersed in this movie
in a way that when it ends,

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:31.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're like,
"What just happened?"

00:01:31.658 --> 00:01:34.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were in some weird time
portal and it's --

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:36.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
It should be
a mandatory screening.

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:38.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everybody should see it just
to see what it was.

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:39.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Fantastic.
Congratulations on it.

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:40.100 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And obviously,
that's "Detroit."

00:01:41.835 --> 00:01:43.970 align:start size:94% position:6%
When we first met,
we're both Red Sox fans.

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:45.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
-In Detroit.
-Met in Detroit.

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:46.239 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We're Red Sox fans.

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:48.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're from Massachusetts.
I'm from New Hampshire.

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:49.309 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's true.

00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:50.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now as someone
from Massachusetts,

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:53.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
do you think it's okay that
somebody from New Hampshire is

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:54.647 align:start size:94% position:6%
also a Red Sox fan?
Do you count us?

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:57.750 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, but, like, you're
like our J.V. squad of fans.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:58.451 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Yeah, okay, gotcha.

00:01:58.451 --> 00:02:00.053 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it's like we ride
in the bus

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:01.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you guys ride in the cars
behind the bus.

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:02.722 line:92%
-That sounds about right.

00:02:02.722 --> 00:02:05.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, you're like,
"Go, Boston Red Sox fans."

00:02:05.058 --> 00:02:06.326 line:92%
We're like, "Thanks, guys."

00:02:06.326 --> 00:02:08.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And yet neither of us --
we are both without accents.

00:02:08.695 --> 00:02:11.030
-It's true.
-Did you have to get rid of one?

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:11.664 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
-Yeah.

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:15.401
-No, I grew up in Newton, Mass.,
which is the least street place,

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:16.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think,
in the suburbs of Boston.

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:19.672
-I should point out,
to the people in actual Boston,

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:21.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
you are the J.V.
-That's right.

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:25.378
-Newton is to like Southie what
New Hampshire is to Newton.

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:26.813 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah.
Right now some guy's going,

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:29.449
"Is he giving that New Hampshire
kid a hard time?

00:02:29.449 --> 00:02:31.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll give you a hard time,
Newton."

00:02:31.284 --> 00:02:32.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's what they're saying
right now.

00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:34.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So you have a Boston accent?
You can do one.

00:02:34.454 --> 00:02:36.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I can dust it off
any time.

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:38.858
-Yeah.
-Usually a couple drinks helps.

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:39.459 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, it does.

00:02:39.459 --> 00:02:41.628
-Or it doesn't even help.
It just forces its way in.

00:02:41.628 --> 00:02:42.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, exactly.
-People are like,

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:45.098
"Oh, when he has drinks,
he does the Boston accent."

00:02:45.098 --> 00:02:47.000 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like,
"No, it's happening now."

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You also -- something else we
have in common.

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:51.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have a couple -- You have
two kids now, two girls.

00:02:51.471 --> 00:02:53.039 line:92%
-Yeah, we're multiplying.

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:53.940 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Beautiful girls.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:55.808
This is interesting to me,
because I'm on the first one.

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:59.412
I've heard you have issues with
the baby products industry.

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:01.014 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You heard from who?
-I've heard --

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:04.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
Look, I've read
some negative Yelp reviews

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:05.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
that are very much
in your voice.

00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:09.189
-That's what it is. Oh, good.
At least you've been tracking.

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:11.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, it's so funny,
you find yourself --

00:03:11.224 --> 00:03:13.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it's the most amazing
thing in the world,

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:15.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you also feel like
you're on duty,

00:03:15.295 --> 00:03:17.430
so you feel kind of stressed out
as far as --

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:18.331 line:92%
You want it to be perfect.

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:21.734
And when they're really young,
little things drove me insane.

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:24.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like wet wipes.
Does anybody have kids?

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:26.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
Nobody has ever had a kid?
-No.

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:28.975
There's these little bags of
wet wipes that you pull out,

00:03:28.975 --> 00:03:30.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you wipe bums,
but the problem is,

00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:31.778 size:84% position:42% line:92%
you never pull out one.

00:03:31.778 --> 00:03:33.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're, like, bunched in 200.
-Yeah.

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:36.449
-So you're holding a kid
that's like seven days old

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:37.383 line:92%
and the first thing she's seeing

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:38.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
is this giant person
being like...

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:40.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Growling ]
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:41.888 line:92%
Like, throwing this thing

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:43.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, like, trying to get
one wet wipe out.

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:46.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
The baby's like,
"This is the worst."

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:47.393 line:92%
Emily's like, "What's going on?"

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:50.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like, "I'm just terrifying
the child, it's fine."

00:03:50.597 --> 00:03:51.998 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And then just last week,

00:03:51.998 --> 00:03:55.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
my youngest daughter
got a onesie

00:03:55.168 --> 00:03:57.103 line:92%
that had color-coded buttons.

00:03:57.103 --> 00:04:00.106
And I had to take a knee.
It was like an emotional moment.

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:02.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
I went, "Thank you
whoever invented this."

00:04:02.008 --> 00:04:02.508 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, yeah.

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:04.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, when a kid's moving
around, you're like,

00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:05.411 size:88% position:44% line:92%
"Where's the button go?"

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:06.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then my kid
gets up like this,

00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:08.081 line:92%
and her shirt's like that.

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:10.283 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There are times where my wife
will be in the other room

00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:12.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
